6.2 Plan in Mbit/sol, not Mbps

The binding constraint is daily volume, not link rate. Continuous 2 Mbps must never be assumed; a 2 Mbps figure multiplied by 86,400 s overestimates daily volume by an order of magnitude.

Storage sizing point: four rovers × ~250 Mbit/sol × 5 sols of autonomy ≈ 5 Gbit onboard storage, with prioritization.

6.3 Relay ownership — undecided

Whether this architecture relies on the aging MRO/MAVEN/TGO fleet or carries its own relay is not decided and must be decided before the manifest is frozen. No relay mass is carried in §2.1. A manifest that depends on the current fleet inherits that fleet's retirement risk.

6.4 Autonomy

Four-level hierarchy retained: mission, site, rover, safety. The N4 safety layer is deterministic and independent of mission software.

Test requirements: simulated relay loss beyond 4 hours triggers a pre-authorized local plan or a safe stop; a rover does not wait for Earth authorization to protect its physical limits; recovery from a safe stop requires cause identification, state verification, and explicit authorization — not a software restart. Safe stop within 10 s.

Status: OPEN. No autonomy code exists; no relay-loss test has been run.

