Zhurong 1.5–6 kPa 21°–34° Ding et al. 2022 

A 2025 review consolidates the full measured range: cohesion 0.10–9.0 kPa, friction angle 18°–35° . MER wheel-trench analyses report cohesions from 0 to 11 kPa in scuffed regolith .

Ratio maximum/minimum ≈ 15 kPa / 0.12 kPa ≈ 125× — two orders of magnitude. A single bearing criterion is indefensible. The geometric verdict and the geotechnical verdict must remain separate.

A.3 Ground pressure versus bearing capacity — the calculation

\text{Ratio} = \frac{15\ \text{kPa}}{2.2\ \text{kPa}} = 6.8

This is not a margin. It is a potential sinkage condition. The risk is never the mean of the distribution; it is the layer that was not tested.

A.4 Cutting force versus traction — the full calculation

Mars gravity: surface acceleration at the equator is 3.71 m/s²; mean surface gravity is 3.73 m/s² . Using 3.71 m/s²:

F_{\text{traction}} = 0.7 \times 2{,}800 \times 3.71 = 7.27\ \text{kN}

Closure criterion:

F_{\text{cut}} \le 0.7 \times F_{\text{traction}} = 0.7 \times 7.27 = \mathbf{5.09\ kN}

Estimated cutting force (simplified McKyes, c ≈ 1.5 kPa, φ = 30°, bucket 0.5 m × 0.15 m): base ≈ 6.1 kN, rising to 7.3–9.1 kN with three-dimensional and dynamic amplification.

\frac{7.3}{5.09} = 1.43 \qquad \frac{9.1}{5.09} = 1.79

The overrun is 1.4–1.8× the closure criterion, not 0.03 kN above gross traction. This is the central correction.

